[about]
Title=5 - Convert Between Formats
Intro=Two wants: a Word document read as text, and Markdown written out as a web page. Opening in another format, exporting to one, and the Markdown preview. This walk assumes walks three and five.
Setup=EdSharp is open, and report.docx is in your Documents folder.
Homework=Open a Word document or a PDF as text, and export a Markdown file as a web page.

[step]

Say=The want: a Word document someone sent, read as text. Control plus Shift plus O, Open Other Format -- Shift widens Open -- converts it on the way in.
Key=Control+Shift+O
Hear=Open Other Format dialog, File name: edit combo

[step]

Say=report dot d o c x, and Enter. EdSharp says what it is doing.
Key=Enter
Hear=Converting
Hear=report dot d o c x, EdSharp
Hear=Quarterly Report
Say=The document is text now: headings are lines, tables are lines, and every key of walks three and five works on it.

[step]

Say=The other direction: writing out as something else. Alt plus Shift plus E, Export Format, offers the formats this document can become.
Key=Alt+Shift+E
Hear=Export Format dialog, Format: list box, Web page, 1 of 8

[step]

Say=Web page, and Enter: the Markdown you are writing becomes an HTML file beside it, and EdSharp says the file.
Key=Enter
Hear=Converted 1 file

[step]

Say=Control plus F9, Preview Markdown, shows the same thing as a formatted page in a window of EdSharp's own, for checking headings and links without leaving the editor.
Key=Control+F9
Hear=Preview, document

[step]

Say=Escape returns. PDF files, slide decks and spreadsheets open the same way, by Control plus Shift plus O; the document tools from the installer's last page are what make the richer ones possible.
Key=Escape
Hear=report dot d o c x, EdSharp

[step]

Say=Control plus T, Text Convert, converts files on disk to text without opening them. List their names in a document, one to a line, and each becomes a text file beside it, ending in dot t x t.
Key=Control+T
Hear=Converted 3 files
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus T, Text Combine, takes the same list but puts every file's text together in one new window, one after another.
Key=Control+Shift+T
Hear=Untitled, edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. The formats on offer depend on what was installed: the document tools from the installer's last page add Word, PDF, EPUB and slide decks; without them, text, Markdown, HTML and RTF are always there.
Key=Escape
Hear=report dot d o c x, EdSharp

[step]

Say=A planned misstep. A PDF that is only a picture of a page -- a scan -- opens as empty or as nonsense, because there is no text in it to convert. The guide's section on PDF says what to do: optical character recognition, which the document tools can run on it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Encoding is the other kind of conversion. A file that opens as symbols where accents should be is in an encoding EdSharp guessed wrong; Alt plus Shift plus Y, Yield Encoding, renders the text in the one you choose, and Alt plus Z twice says the encoding in use.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Markdown to plain text, HTML to Markdown, a table in a document to lines you can read -- each is an export or an open-other-format away, and the preview, Control plus F9, is the check before you send.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Where converted files go. Open Other Format reads the original and makes a text copy in your temporary folder; Save puts it where you say. Export writes beside the original, with the new extension; Text Convert does the same for files on disk.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Tables come through as lines: each row is a line, each cell separated by a tab or a bar, which a reader reads better than a grid. Headings keep their level as Markdown's pound signs, so Control plus B and the heading keys still move by them.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=A planned misstep. Export to PDF with the document tools not installed, and EdSharp says so and names the box on the installer's last page that provides them; nothing hangs and nothing half-converts.
Key=
Hear=PDF export needs the document tools. Run the installer and tick Document tools.

[step]

Say=Images in a document are listed by their alternative text, when the author gave any; a document with none says image and its file name, which is itself a finding when you are checking someone's accessibility.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Round trips are safe: a Markdown file exported to Word and opened again as text returns as the same Markdown, headings and lists intact; what is lost is only what Markdown cannot say, such as a font.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus O.
Key=
Hear=Open Other Format

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus E.
Key=
Hear=Export Format

[step]

Say=Control plus F9.
Key=
Hear=Preview Markdown
